# moon_supply

Keep a Moon AE2 watchlist at target counts by exporting from Earth AE2 into the Interplanetary Railgun Sender, then firing under Earth-controller command. Moon unloads itself. Items only (no fluids).

## Non-goals

- Fluids; full AE2-Moon dump; Moon receiver control
- In-flight accounting (flight 60 s, send pause 80 s; the next poll sees Moon AE already updated)
- Legacy fire-by-full as the primary mode for this sender (use `moon_supply` earth; standalone `railgun` is manual/legacy)

## Layout

### Earth (`entries/moon_supply_E_ctrl.lua`)

- Computer on wired net + ender modem **bottom**
- `meBridge_2` on AE2-Earth; exports straight into HV loaders via `exportItemToPeripheral` (optional `buffer` chest only if leftovers exist)
- Loaders: `tfg:hv_railgun_item_loader_in_20` … `_29` (`loader_prefix`, `expected | 10`)
- `redstone_relay` **top**, pulse **`back`**
- `monitor_1` — Moon stock / phase UI

### Moon (`entries/moon_supply_M_probe.lua`)

- Computer, ender modem **top**, ME Bridge on the **right** side (`bridge | right`)
- Stock probe only: answers Earth’s `stock_req` with `getItem` counts (no local watchlist)
- Railgun receiver unloads into Moon AE without this computer

## Behaviour

1. Poll Moon stocks: Earth sends watchlist ids in `stock_req`; Moon replies `stock_res` (protocol `tfg_moon_supply`). One source of truth — Earth’s cfg. Moon warms a full `getItem` cache once, then refreshes a rotating slice (~6 ids/req) so replies stay short on large ME.
2. Per item: `red_line = floor(target * red_frac)` (default `0.25`).
   - **ALARM** (global) if **any** item has `moon < red_line`
   - **WARN** if no ALARM but any `moon < target`
   - **OK** → idle
3. Build a shot package from deficits. Within a zone, cfg order. In **ALARM**, alarm items load before warn items of the same shot. **WARN** sends warn deficits only. Mid-shot, `mergePackage` expands wants from fresh Moon assess (e.g. gold dips while diamond crafts) — never shrinks in-flight wants.
4. Missing on Earth: try `craftItem` on the **final** item (AE expands multi-step trees itself). Prefer full ask →256→64→16→1; verify CPU job. Ghost success (`API ok` without a job) stops size fallback immediately. Keep topping up crafts after wait-collapse until the package deficit is covered. Hard fails (`NOT_CRAFTABLE` / `not craftable` / `ITEM_NOT_FOUND`) set `craftStatus=no`. Soft fails (`API ok, no AE job` / `craft returned nil`): 8 s cooldown, after 2 in a shot → `craftStatus=fail`. `effectiveCraft` clamps AE craft vs earth+staged; opaque `craftKnown=false` shows `Крафт (1)` only while the row is still short. Row status blinks `Крафт (n)` ↔ `Загружено (m)` (1 s each, orange/yellow) when both inbound and loaded; sys line shows live `крафт AE N в работе`, not a dead 60 s countdown.
5. After the first craft probe, **unobtainable** ids (`craftStatus` no/fail or AE not craftable) are dropped from the shot even if some cargo is already staged (remainder does not block fire). If nothing remains, **no craft-wait / no launch prep** — idle + status `не шлём (нет в AE): …`.
6. During craft-wait (**ALARM 60 s** / **WARN 120 s**, or **3 s** if no AE jobs) only for obtainable items: export AE → loaders (stock/`earth>0` first; skip full loaders; ~2 s cooldown after a zero-move so focus snaps do not re-spam); re-request craft as needed. **Collapse wait as soon as AE CPUs are idle** (sticky `req`/pending no longer holds the full timer after craft finishes). Title stays short (`сборка` / `загрузка`); status lines say `крафт AE` / `сборка пакета` / `выгрузка`. Debug ring under the table shows timings.
7. **Fire** when the obtainable shot package sits in the loaders, or when every loader is cargo-full — but **not** while Earth still has obtainable stock/craft to push (`moreToLoad`). WARN zone rules unchanged; this only blocks early fire (e.g. diamond done, gold just merged). `загрузка` title only when loaders actually hold cargo. If the package cannot be finished after the wait, return to poll with a status note.
8. Pulse relay → `cooldown | 80`. Flight is 60 s, so the next poll sees the delivery. No in-flight reserve. A failed relay pulse does not start the cooldown.
9. **Parallel runtime**: `uiLoop` + `aeWatchLoop` + `moonWatchLoop` + `controlLoop`. Moon watch owns ender stock probes; control reads the cache (no competing rednet). AE watch refreshes Земля/Крафт (focus=active package; full every 8th, or every 12th when watchlist ≥30; slower when idle). Control exports/crafts/fires without owning long AE/Moon scans. `requestCrafts` schedules **all** short package items in one pass, accounts for in-flight crafting (clamped), retries every 2 s. Snapshot: crafting-tasks first, `getItem` with sparse `sleep(0)` yields.

